 "note": "Busselton War Memorial, Victoria Square (1919-20), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and the State heritage record. A Donnybrook sandstone and limestone obelisk on a stepped base with a grey granite name tablet, in the middle of a raised square of pale paving with low hedged planters at its corners and a path in from the north. South of it a second smaller paved square between long planters, then a path on to the south. The RSL built a new memorial in Rotary Park in 2024; this one is still in the square on the aerial. Front = north, to the street. Metres: x east to west as seen from the street, y south from the obelisk.",
